---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { officialRegisters } from "../data/directory";
---

<Base
  title="Official sources | Andorra Private"
  description="Where Andorran residency, tax, banking, healthcare, education and property licences are published: Govern.ad, AFA, AGIA, CADA, CASS, SAAS and Andorran Banking."
  path="/official-sources"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Official sources</h1>
    <p>
      A short map of the public registers. We do not repeat fees, quotas or
      investment figures here — those change, and only the live official text is
      safe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        This page is an index, not advice. Open the official site for the
        current procedure. For named firms we have already sourced, use the
        <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Immigration and residence</h2>
    <p>
      The Servei d’Immigració publishes residence-and-work and residence-without-work
      authorisations on
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
      >. Letter codes such as A.1, J.1 and D.1 are the Government’s own. Read
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      for orientation, then the live pages.
    </p>

    <h2>Tax and finance</h2>
    <p>
      The
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/ministeris-i-secretaries-d-estat/ministeri-de-finances"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Ministeri de Finances</a
      >
      and the taxes-and-customs theme on Govern.ad are the public tax sources.
      The
      <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Andorran Financial Authority</a
      >
      supervises the financial system. We do not quote rates.
    </p>

    <h2>Banks</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.andorranbanking.ad/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Andorran Banking</a
      >
      is the association of Andorran banks. It currently lists three groups —
      Andbank, MoraBanc and Creand — which we also list in the directory. Opening
      an account is a compliance process described by each bank and by the AFA.
    </p>

    <h2>Property licences</h2>
    <p>
      Licensed estate agents are listed by
      <a href="https://www.agia.ad/collegiats" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >AGIA</a
      >, the professional college. We only name firms that appear there and
      publish their own site. See
      <a href="/properties">how we list homes</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Lawyers</h2>
    <p>
      Practising advocates are organised through the
      <a href="https://www.cada.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Col·legi d’Advocats d’Andorra</a
      >. Confirm a name on that register before you instruct anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>Health and social security</h2>
    <p>
      Public care is described by
      <a href="https://saas.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SAAS</a>;
      affiliation and benefits by
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASS</a>.
      A short reading is on
      <a href="/healthcare">healthcare</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
      The Government publishes the three education systems — Andorran, Spanish
      and French — on its
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/educacio-formacio-investigacio-i-divulgacio-del-coneixement/estudiar-a-andorra/sistemes-educatius-a-andorra"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">education pages</a
      >. See
      <a href="/education">education</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>High-intent notes on this site</h2>
    <p>
      Longer English readings that only restate official pages:
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra">moving to Andorra</a>,
      <a href="/opening-a-bank-account">opening a bank account</a>,
      <a href="/buying-property">buying property</a>,
      <a href="/residence-without-work">D.1</a>,
      <a href="/digital-nomad">D.3</a>,
      <a href="/entrepreneur-residence">D.4</a>,
      <a href="/self-employed-residence">J.1</a>,
      <a href="/family-reunification">B.1</a>,
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
      Jane Whittaker’s whole
      <a
        href="https://www.livinginandorra.com/index.html"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">livinginandorra.com</a
      >
      site is a standing English practitioner map, listed at
      <a href="/directory/jane-whittaker">J W Serveis</a>
      and read against official text on
      <a href="/practitioner-map">the practitioner-map page</a>
      — not a BOPA text.
    </p>

    <h2>The full list we use</h2>
    <div class="official-links">
      {
        officialRegisters.map((reg) => (
          <a href={reg.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            {reg.name} — {reg.note}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
